course: dictionary
lesson: 8086
title: Re- words: remarry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The little word re- at the start of a word often means again. Read, redo and rewrite all work this way. Remarry is built the same way: re- means again, and marry means to become husband and wife.
explain: So remarry means to marry again. «Remarrying means marrying again after a divorce or after a husband or wife has died.» Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "marrying again after a divorce" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Remarry is a grown-up word, and you may meet it in a story or in a family. «When a parent marries again (remarries), the new husband or wife becomes the child's step-parent, so a child can have a dad and a stepdad.» The clues show that remarries and marries again mean the same thing.
fact: Re- often means again, as in redo, reread and remarry.
fact: Marry means to become husband and wife; remarry means to marry again.
fact: Someone can remarry after a divorce, or after their husband or wife has died.
fact: When a parent remarries, the new husband or wife is the child's step-parent, such as a stepdad or stepmum.
fact: Remarry is a verb: remarry, remarries, remarried, remarrying. For example: "They remarried last spring."
exercise: What does remarry mean? | To make a new friend | To leave school early | To move house | *To marry again
exercise: «When a parent marries again (remarries), the new husband or wife becomes the child's step-parent.» What is a step-parent? | A child who lives with a grandparent | *The new husband or wife of a child's parent | A teacher at school | A parent who has never been married
exercise: In «Remarrying means marrying again after a divorce», which words mean the same as remarrying? | Forgetting the wedding | Being divorced | *Marrying again | Leaving the house
test: The prefix re- means again. What does redo mean? | Do before | *Do again | Stop doing | Do nothing
test: Sam's dad remarried last year. What has happened? | *Sam's dad got married again | Sam's dad moved abroad | Sam's dad got divorced | Sam's dad got a new job
exam: Which sentence uses remarry correctly? | Remarry the bus to school | He remarry yesterday at the shop | *After the divorce, she decided to remarry two years later | She remarry her cat every morning
